e county&rsquo;s 6 grids in Jersey County has 75 years on record, and November to December came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 27% of normal in August to September and 140% in June to July. Every grid had its driest year in 1953, with grid 22659 lowest at 58%. On grid 22658 the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 sits at 86.6, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
